            <ArticleTitle>Laser laparoscopic surgery in the treatment of ovarian endometriomas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To assess the efficacy of laser laparoscopic photocoagulation of endometriomas (2-18 cm) in patients with pain, infertility, or a combination of the two.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Retrospective review of all patients with endometriomas from June 1, 1983, to December 31, 1993.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">Department of gynecology and obstetrics at a district general hospital and national training center in minimal access surgery.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">One hundred sixty-five women with large endometriomas present at the time of laser laparoscopy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Carbon dioxide laser or potassium-titanyl-phosphate laser laparoscopic surgery.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Ninety (74%) of 122 patients reported improvement or resolution of pain; and 30 of 66 achieved a pregnancy, for a cumulative conception rate of 45%.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Laser laparoscopy is a practical, safe, and effective technique for the management of large ovarian endometriomas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
